{"name":"Biscotti","hex":"#d8c3a7","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"biscotti","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard, usually nut-flavored biscuit, derived from the Tuscan cantuccio."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of biscotto"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/biscotti"}],"entries":[{"title":"Biscotti","blocks":[{"text":"Biscotti are Italian almond biscuits originating in the city of Prato, Tuscany. They are twice-baked, oblong-shaped, dry, and crunchy. In Italy, they are known as cantucci, biscotti di Prato or biscotti etruschi and may be dipped in a drink, traditionally Vin Santo. Smaller biscotti may be known as biscottini or cantuccini. In Italian, the word biscotti encompasses all types of biscuits or cookies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Cantuccini-Toscani.jpg/330px-Cantuccini-Toscani.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biscotti","wikidata":"Q769635"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/I_cantuccini.jpg/500px-I_cantuccini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/I_cantuccini.jpg/1280px-I_cantuccini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/I_cantuccini.jpg/500px-I_cantuccini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Almond cantuccini","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AI_cantuccini.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Pignoli_biscotti_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Pignoli_biscotti_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Pignoli_biscotti_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-